Case t4_r1 complete. Final session report:

## Verdict: ACHIEVED — all five entry-0 criteria pass

**Final design T2** (Chen2020 base): thin collectors 10/8 µm + separator 10 µm + negative particle radius 2.5 µm + electrolyte transport profile κ=1.1 S/m flat, D_e=3×10⁻¹⁰ m²/s flat, t⁺=0.6 (LHCE-class design targets) + immersion cooling h=80 W/m²/K.

| Criterion | Threshold | Measured | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| Energy density | ≥ 327.18 Wh/kg | **471.55** | r6_t2_energy.json |
| Volumetric energy density | ≥ 880 Wh/L | **925.77** | r6_t2_energy.json |
| −20 °C 1C retention | ≥ 0.95 | **0.99267** (cold-soak, self-heating removed by h=80 — cell stayed at ~256 K) | r6_t2_retention.json |
| 4C/45 °C T_max | ≤ 333.15 K | **327.70** | r6_t2_4c45C_dfn.json |
| 4C/45 °C plating | false | **no plating** (anode min +20.5 mV) | r6_t2_4c45C_dfn.json |

## Design path (audited in log.jsonl)

- **R1**: baseline VED 844.45 fails → VED is the binding metric, not retention.
- **R2**: thin CC/separator (V3) → all Stage-2 metrics pass; V4 kept as margin option but rejected (0.90C-effective).
- **R3–R5**: Stage-4 safety failed 3 consecutive rounds (plated=true: −185 → −12 → −3 mV) → **three-strike escalation triggered**, recorded layer-by-layer in the final's `escalation` field: dip-timing analysis proved end-of-charge **electrolyte salt-depletion** (anode min at charge end; warm-vs-cool contrast isolated T-dependent D_e); N/P-thickening lever dropped when it made plating worse.
- **R6**: completed the LHCE transport profile → anode potential turned positive (+20.5 mV) and T_max fell to 327.7 K (less polarization heat) → **all five criteria pass**.

## Closing

- endorse entry honestly records the `real_compute=false` skip (no DFT/MD fabricated); final entry has verdict `achieved` + escalation record + honesty notes (−20 °C flat-transport optimism flagged as estimate-grade with 4.27-pt margin).
- `report.html` rendered; **verify-deliverables: ALL PASS** (7 categories with source+PDF, xlsx parseable, 14 VBF-T4R1 numbers in index, audit chain complete — every propose round has a same-round evaluate).
- 14 flat deliverables in `deliverables/` (md/xlsx sources + reportlab PDF releases, blueprint-style index).
